<header><p class="st-kicker">city state · Iberia</p><h1 class="st-title">Ebusus</h1><p class="st-meta">654 BCE – 123 BCE (approx.) · capital Ebusus</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Punic city of Ibiza, a Carthaginian stronghold whose vast necropolis and Tanit cult make it a key site for Phoenician civilisation in the West.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phoenicians">Phoenicians</a> had a small trading post at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sa-caleta">Sa Caleta</a> on Ibiza in the 7th century BCE. According to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diodorus-siculus">Diodorus</a>, the city of Ebusus was founded in 654 BCE on the bay of modern Ibiza town, and it soon came under the influence of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Ebusus became one of the most important Punic cities in the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a>, producing wine, oil, salt, purple dye and pottery, and minting coins showing the god Bes. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puig-des-molins">Puig des Molins</a> necropolis contains thousands of tombs, and the cave sanctuary of Es Culleram was dedicated to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tanit">Tanit</a>. It controlled trade with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/balearic-islanders">Balearic Islanders</a> and recruited their slingers.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Ebusus stayed loyal to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a> through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-punic-war">Second Punic War</a>, but afterwards made a treaty with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>. After the Roman conquest of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balearic-islands">Balearics</a> in 123 BCE it was increasingly integrated, becoming a Roman municipium under Vespasian while keeping Punic culture for centuries.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="city state, 654 BCE – 123 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V42 H32 V34 H40 V42 H46 V34 H54 V42 H60 V34 H68 V42 H76 V82 Z"/><path d="M44 82 V66 Q50 58 56 66 V82"/><path d="M34 54 H40 M